%N A400097 Numbers k such that the trajectory of k->ord(4,k) reaches 1 before reaching a number not coprime to 4. Here ord(b,k) is the multiplicative order of b modulo k.
%C A400097 Closed under multiplication; see A400096 for details.
%H A400097 Jianing Song, <a href="/A400097/b400097.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 1..10000</a>
%e A400097 Powers of 3 are terms: 3^n -> 3^(n-1) -> ... -> 3 -> 1;
%e A400097 43 is a term: 43 -> 7 -> 3 -> 1.
%t A400097 (* okQ is defined at A400096 *)
%t A400097 Select[Range[1200], okQ[#, 4] &] (* _Paolo Xausa_, Nov 26 2026 *)
%o A400097 (PARI) isok(n, 4) \\ see A400096 for isok
%Y A400097 See A400096 for list of sequences in other bases.
